      "details": {
        "goal": "Design a question that asks whether two observed outputs are both moving. Change one visible connection so the previously blocked branch can move, while motion at the other output can still be inferred independently. Keep the input, question and four options the same.",
        "sources": [
          "MentalAnimation/MechanicalSystem/Level0/10",
          "MentalAnimation/MechanicalSystem/Level0/12",
          "MentalAnimation/MechanicalSystem/Level0/34",
          "MentalAnimation/MechanicalSystem/Level1/6"
        ],
        "change": "Switch the working face at contact 1 from the far bank to the near bank. The rendered local section changes the B CW tangent arrow from leftward to rightward while the A CW tangent still points right.",
        "reason": "A turns CW, so its active face travels along the rightward A CW tangent. At contact 1 the B CW tangent points left. Matching contact velocity requires B to turn CCW. Contact 2 overruns under B CCW. The holding brake arrests C. On the other branch, contact 3 is a solid key, so K turns CW. Its upper pin travels right, and contact 4 transmits the pin's horizontal component to Y.",
        "expectedChecks": [
          "The filled pinion and far label coincide at flag 1. The near seat is open. The CW arrows oppose. Flags 2–4 identify the brake-equipped clutch, rigid key, and pin in the yoke. All answer choices and output labels are visible.",
          "Blind read C / C stationary / Y right."
        ]
      },
      "evidenceRefs": []
